WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.310
<i>It is the near future.</i>

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.980
<i>To stand against the apparitions called O'bli</i>

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>that appear from distortions in space-time,</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.030
<i>a group of girls were assembled 
to fight, unknown to the public.</i>

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>This is a story of the love, 
courage, and friendship</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>shared by a group of girls called Strikers.</i>

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.040
<b>Train! And Our First Victory</b>

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.740
Altair Torte has returned to base.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.090
Welcome back.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.090
We're back.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.710
Good work, moshu.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.530
I had Coconut Vega, 
who was patrolling nearby,

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.230
head there for backup.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.770
I'm glad they made it in time.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.480
That's why they got there so fast!

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.750
Their timing was so good,

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.700
I thought they'd been hiding 
somewhere waiting for their turn.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.530
That'd be even more impressive.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.620
We're sorry our lack of experience 
caused so much trouble.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.680
Altair Torte has only just been formed.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.880
Just try your best next time.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.020
Understood.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.250
Your contributions have been registered,

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.050
and you've been given points, moshu.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.760
Hear that? We still get points, 
even if we had help!

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.890
Y-Yeah.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.240
Only a few, though...

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.270
Hey, Satoka-chan, 
you're not supposed to say that!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.770
Then, please excuse us.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.940
Hey, Tsubame.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.440
We'll have to thank the girls in Coconut Vega.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.410
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.280
Well, I'll talk to you later.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.420
I wonder if Altair Torte is 
going to be okay, moshu.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.360
They'll be fine.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:21.260
They just haven't realized 
their own potential yet.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.380
Moshu?

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.280
Tsubame seems kind of down.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.580
You think so?

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.390
I'm sure it was a shock that she couldn't 
defeat the O'bli on her own.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.870
Maybe Tsubame-chan is feeling more 
responsibility because she's the leader.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.410
Io-chin, can you go home today?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.840
Yeah. Practice is off.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.340
Yay!

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.460
What's up?

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.400
Let's go home.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.570
Oh, Yuumi-chin, Sato-chin, listen to this!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.670
What's going on?

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.520
How about we all stop somewhere first?

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.190
Miyama-san.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.520
Tierra-sensei.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.360
Looking at battle reports?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.300
Yes.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.760
I was thinking about how we could get 
closer in performance to the other teams.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:26.660
I'm sorry.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.530
Huh?

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.380
It was me, the Time-Space Administrator,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.290
who judged you to have the 
most potential as a leader

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.700
when Altair Torte was formed.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.550
That's not something you 
need to apologize for.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:45.850
But I thought that was 
something you needed to do.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.220
In order to find yourself again.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.430
Yeah...

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.230
Do you still not feel like going to school?

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.390
Sorry for causing so much trouble.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.690
No!

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:06.480
I can easily transfer you in 
at any time, if I wanted to.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.280
R-Right...

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.030
What about the others?

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:11.730
Huh?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.540
School's already out, right?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.300
Y-Yeah.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.830
They contacted me earlier 
saying they'd be a bit late

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.550
because they wanted to go shopping.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:24.700
Shopping?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.490
Potential as a leader, huh?

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.670
Tsubame-chin!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.810
See? I told you she'd be here!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.060
What? I'm the one who said that.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.810
When we went to your room, no one 
was there, so we went looking for you.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.340
Sorry.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.570
Did you go shopping?

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.610
Yeah.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.990
We got permission from Tierra—I mean,
 Yukako-sensei—to leave campus.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.070
I see.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.130
It must be nice being able to go out.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.500
What is it?

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.390
One, two...

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.340
Ta-da!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:06.920
What are those?

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.040
These are what we went shopping for.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.660
There are so many.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.330
It was Mana's idea.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:26.230
I remembered when Sato-chin said we 
should eat some good food to cheer up.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:26.860
Huh?

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.550
Good food is justice.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:36.870
So we're having an "Everyone eats good food 
with Tsubame-chan to cheer her up" party.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.770
You guys...

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:43.740
Now, let's have this "Everyone eats 
good food with Tsubame-chin"...

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.250
Uh, what was it again?

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.760
"Everyone eats good food with 
Tsubame-chan to cheer her up" party.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:50.720
That's what it was.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.130
That's too long!

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:56.420
That's funny.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.260
You don't have to laugh so much.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.470
We'll shorten it to the "EveryTsuba" party.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:01.980
I like that!

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.350
I want to eat both of these...

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.630
Hey, Satoka-chan, don't you think 
you got too much curry bead?

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.540
No need to worry.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:12.990
Huh?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.220
If there are any left over,

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:18.360
I'll take responsibility and deal with them.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.660
You plan to eat all of them, don't you?

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.550
Come on, let's eat.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.670
Okay.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.920
Getting depressed won't 
help you move forward.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.800
You're right.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:30.980
Thanks.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.060
Move forward, huh?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:44.020
Coconut Vega was pretty impressive.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.140
Even if we can't surpass Hazuki-san and the rest,

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.180
I want to at least reach their level...

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.160
That's it!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.450
Training?

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.360
Yeah.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.460
I think our team, Altair Torte,

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:07.790
is lacking experience compared 
to the rest of the teams.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.260
Well, that's because our team 
was the last created.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.850
That's to be expected.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.930
That's why I was thinking we could 
make up for that lack through training.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.010
That sounds great.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.460
Nice idea.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.310
What would we do for this training?

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:30.600
Well, I was thinking we could 
all think about that together.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.530
So stuff like push-ups and sit-ups for starters?

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.950
For starters? That would make me bulk up...

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.610
You'd get all muscly.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:41.040
Huh?! I don't want that!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.070
Well, we would need flexibility, too.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:47.420
Also, good balance.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.160
Also instantaneous force 
and dynamic visual acuity.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.550
But I think food is important 
in building a healthy body.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.890
Yeah, that's true.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.890
So, Yuumi-san, you're going to 
be in charge of cooking.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.960
Roger!

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.310
Just leave it to me!

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.600
So what are we doing to do, Tsubame?

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:10.740
We can try all of it and then decide.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.260
That's the spirit!

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:50.600
Huh?

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:51.740
Where's Yuumi?

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.570
She's doing her job.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:57.150
Lobster roast with sauce américaine!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.780
Duck breast meat poêlé 
with an orange-based sauce!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.340
This is good!

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.920
You made all of this, Yuumi?

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.510
It wasn't me.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:18.800
The Chef Cuisinière Sajima-san 
used his great skill to make it.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.680
Cuisinière?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.510
That's right.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.900
There was a mysterious chef just passing by.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.810
There's plenty more, so eat up.

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:32.520
This is pretty good, 
but my body hurts all over.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.070
You'll get used to it eventually.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.910
And you'll get all muscly!

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.470
Oh, no!

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:42.160
All right! I'm going to get all muscly, then!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.100
If you put on muscles,

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.370
you'll put on weight, 
which'll make you more stable.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:47.660
I don't want that.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.410
I'm not going to get muscly anymore.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.290
What's wrong with looking tough?

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:51.960
Right?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.210
Y-Yeah...

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:58.160
Now, let's eat up and 
train more and get muscly!

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.510
Yeah!

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.600
I don't want to be muscly!

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.650
I said I wanted us to train,

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.810
but I'm not sure this is really working.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:25.330
You were awake?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.030
Yeah.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.700
Look!

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:33.180
I came up with a training 
regimen for tomorrow.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.620
Take a look.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.090
A training regimen?

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.760
Huh...

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.640
There's even swimming.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.300
Yeah. It works out the entire body,

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.270
and it's a good change of pace.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.310
That's true.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:48.800
I'm impressed.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.980
You were able to put this together so fast.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.650
I'm good at this stuff. 
I'm on the volleyball team, after all.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:57.860
But practice was hard at first.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.110
Huh? Hard for you?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.220
Of course it was.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.500
But now that I think back on it,

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.280
I think I really enjoyed all 
of it, even the hard parts.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.620
People's memories aren't 
very reliable, are they?

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.350
Memories...

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.290
You still can't remember, huh?

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:24.470
I wish I could at least remember
where I came from, but...

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.400
The first thing I noticed then

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.900
was a building floating in front of me.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:40.190
And then a weird cleaning robot flew at me.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.480
It saved me.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:45.220
A weird cleaning robot...

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.750
You mean Moshune-chan?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:49.560
Don't tell Moshune-chan I said that.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.440
Oh, could I borrow that?

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.220
That's right.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:58.850
I wanted to show you this.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:00.520
Here you go.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.550
Is this from the other day?

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:05.760
Yeah.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:11.060
I thought it'd be best to observe how the 
other team fought and learn from that.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.900
And so, I realized something.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.850
First they confuse the enemy with an attack,

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:20.770
and then they stop it from moving.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:24.440
They hit it directly to inflict damage,

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.570
and finish it off with missiles.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:30.980
See?

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:34.500
They're using an attack pattern 
to ensure they take it out.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.500
So we can't just attack randomly, then.

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.900
Thank you, Io.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:40.960
Huh? For what?

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:46.140
I was worried about whether this 
training plan I randomly came up with

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.130
would really work out...

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:51.320
Don't worry about that.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:54.560
Everyone wants to get stronger.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.040
Anyway, sorry for coming over so late.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.020
It's okay. Thanks so much.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.100
No matter where you came from,

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:11.290
you'll always be an important friend to us.

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:12.990
Io...

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:16.240
Anyway, goodnight, Leader.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.750
An attack pattern?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.840
Yeah, let's think about it 
while we continue working out.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.550
But what should we do?

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.380
I can't really think of anything.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.430
We have to figure out everyone's positions,

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.440
their distance, how they attack...

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.480
Our positions and how we attack...

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.900
That's it!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.860
I have a great idea!

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:50.820
How's this?

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.160
Still low on the right, I think.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.580
Okay, just keep holding it.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:58.590
Take a look, Sato-chin.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.120
It's very expressive. Just like you.

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.300
Yay! I got praised!

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.550
Something like this, I think...

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:12.250
What are you all doing?

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.350
Tierra-sensei.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.740
Training to get stronger, of course.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.520
Training?

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.310
Yes, that's right.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.820
Dum da-dum!

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.320
We're about to begin!

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:28.070
Roar! I'm an O'bli.

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.170
Let's get him!

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:30.320
Bang, bang!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.060
Ha, ha, ha! That's not going to work!

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.130
Darn it!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:35.410
Bang, bang!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.140
Are you okay, Mana-chan?!

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:38.460
Yuumi-chin!

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.580
Bang!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:40.770
Ha, ha, ha!

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:42.240
It's useless!

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.480
There's an opening!

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.880
Tsubame, go around from behind!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.880
R-Right!

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.780
H-Hold on.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:50.510
Huh?

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.880
There's no room back here.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.390
Huh?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.610
Hey! Don't push!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.830
I'm going to change my position.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:15:59.980
R-Right.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:00.810
I can't breathe.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.450
H-Hold on.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.350
This isn't going to...

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.680
Ow...

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.040
Is everyone okay?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.450
Just what are you training for?

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.210
We're fighting the O'bli. It's a simula—

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:19.280
Simu—

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:20.130
Simula—

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.660
A simulation?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.160
Yeah, that's it!

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:26.120
You know, you should take this seriously—

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.360
We are being serious.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:31.110
We all thought of a plan.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:34.220
I know it looks like we were 
just playing around, but...

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.480
A plan?

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.390
Yes.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.890
I think we were just fighting without 
thinking of anything up until now.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:45.630
But we realized that we could never
defeat a strong O'bli that way.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.650
So you decided to create a plan instead?

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.360
I thought of it!

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:50.960
I see.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:56.160
It's not a bad thing that you all 
worked together to create a plan.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.410
I'm not sure you're going about 
it the right way, though.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.490
What?!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.940
It was going well up until that last part...

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.220
Guess we'll just have to 
use our bodies to practice.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:09.130
Let's do it.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:10.830
Let's do this, Tsubame.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:12.800
Yeah.

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.460
A dimensional anomaly in R-Sector, moshu.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:19.760
A real O'bli?

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:22.470
Fifth Force! Move out!

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:23.980
Right!

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.660
We could've gotten our formation 
down with a bit more work.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.150
We're being thrown straight into battle?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.060
Will we be okay?

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.910
It should go fine, theoretically.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.180
Here I go!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.000
Yeah!

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.420
Let's go!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.050
All right!

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.260
Come.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.860
Altair Torte has arrived at R-Sector.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:01.740
<i>There are O'bli appearing 
at several points, moshu.</i>

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.620
<i>The dimensional distortions are still there.</i>

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:06.740
Be careful.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:07.540
Roger.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.340
Around here?

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.420
There's nothing here.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.080
Over there!

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.800
A dimensional distortion!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:19.010
An O'bli!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.060
We have a Magire O'bli!

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.010
A new type, moshu!

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:24.720
The other teams?

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.310
They're currently fighting 
in other areas, moshu.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:28.810
It's fast!

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:38.820
What is this?

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.080
Our weapons...

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:41.200
They're different from before!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:43.910
Wow!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.400
<i>That's because of Memoca.</i>

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:48.240
Memoca?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.210
It's when you temporarily borrow power from

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.460
your other self in the parallel world, moshu.

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.610
In order to use Memoca,

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:59.590
you need the experience and ability for it.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.440
That means...

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:03.220
It must be because of our training!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.090
This is amazing!

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.690
Way to go, Leader.

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:07.560
Yeah.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.360
If you all get stronger,

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.100
you'll be able to use stronger Memoca.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:14.960
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:15.870
Yeah!

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:20.940
Let's give this a try, then.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.240
What's that?

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.830
We don't want to approach that carelessly.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:30.500
There we go.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:32.160
Mana, do it now!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.920
Here I go!

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:39.670
Th-That's a lot of power.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.800
Let's do it, Tsubame-chan!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:43.260
Huh?

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:44.590
The plan.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.590
Trying it without practice sounds good!

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:49.810
It kind of sounds like us.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.840
Tierra-sensei, watch this.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:53.350
Moshu?

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.940
This is what we trained for!

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:58.520
We're going to take out...

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.190
...this O'bli!

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:05.140
Formation: Puppet Dance!

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.950
(We're still working on the name)!

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.710
Wow! Wow!

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:21.660
The plan totally worked!

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:23.420
We did it, Tsubame!

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:24.300
Yeah.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:25.590
We did it.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.100
Okay, we're doing swimming today.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.610
We're still training?

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:37.350
I don't want to get any more muscly.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:43.060
Everyone's exhausted after that fight.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:44.940
And swimming, of all things...

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:49.990
Well, we've learned we have a lot less 
stamina than the other teams.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:54.000
You just have to train, a little at a time, 
without rushing to the goal.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:57.550
Okay, do ten laps of crawl strokes.

00:21:57.550 --> 00:21:59.000
What?!

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:01.960
Ready... Start!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:04.570
All right, I'm gonna do this!

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:05.920
I won't lose!

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.940
<b>Formed! Altair Torte</b>

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:40.420
"Formed! Altair Torte."
